// c74_madd (ROADMAP A2b step 2a guard): the MADD fold in vs_try_madd. Freezes the four
// shapes that decide whether `a * b + c` may collapse into the multiply's own word:
//   x  mul then add, addend a permanent symbol register (the fold fires)
//   y  the operands in the other order, `c + a * b` (fires -- `+` is commutative and the
//      fold looks at both window entries, not just the top)
//   z  two multiplies under one `+`, only the LAST of which is still the last word emitted
//      (fires on that one; the first mul is an ordinary REG operand by then)
//   w  the multiplicand is itself computed, `a * (b + c) + b` (fires: the inner `+` is
//      emitted before the mul, so the mul is still the last word when the outer `+` lands)
// and one shape that must NOT fold: `v * b + 4242` materialises its addend with a movz,
// which would land AFTER the mul and be read a word before it was written -- the addend's
// entry is a CONST, not one of vs_reg's is_direct kinds, so the fold declines and
// vs_binop_reg emits the plain add. All five are folded into one printed value so a
// regression in any of them moves the number.
// EXPECT 82837312 from: hand: multiply-add folding (A2b step 2a - from tools/bpref.py)
fn main() -> i64 {
  let a = 7;
  let b = 11;
  let c = 5;
  let x = a * b + c;
  let y = c + a * b;
  let z = a * b + a * c;
  let w = a * (b + c) + b;
  let v = a * b + 4242;
  x * 1000003 + y * 10007 + z * 101 + w * 7 + v
}
